@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+# Stock reservations — spec
+
+## Why
+
+Checkout needs to hold stock for a cart while the customer pays. Once payment
+succeeds, the hold becomes an order. If payment fails, the hold is released.
+Carts get abandoned, so a hold that nobody confirms must give its stock back
+by itself, without a background job. The cart service retries calls, so
+reserving again with the same idempotency key must never create a second hold.
+
+The default hold length is 20 minutes because checkout data shows 95% of
+payments finish within 18 minutes.
+
+## Interface (fixed)
+
+`InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` keeps working exactly as it does
+today.
+
+- `InventoryService.reserve(warehouse: str, items: dict[str, int], idempotency_key: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.confirm_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Order`
+- `InventoryService.release_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.get_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.available(sku, warehouse)` must take holds into account.
+- `inventory.models`: dataclass `Reservation` with `reservation_id: str`,
+  `warehouse: str`, `items: dict[str, int]` (units held per SKU),
+  `status: ReservationStatus`, `expires_at: datetime`, `order_id: str | None`;
+  enum `ReservationStatus` with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`,
+  `EXPIRED`.
+- `inventory.errors`: new `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`,
+  `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` (all subclass
+  `InventoryError`); reuse the existing errors where they fit.
+- Time comes only from the injected clock. There is no background job: expiry
+  must take effect without anyone calling a sweep.
+
+## Terms
+
+- **Hold**: units a reservation sets aside for one SKU in one warehouse.
+- **Active hold**: a hold on a reservation that is `ACTIVE` and has not
+  lapsed, meaning `clock.now() < expires_at`.
+- **Available**: `on_hand − allocated − active holds` for each SKU in each
+  warehouse, never below 0. **Allocated** still means only units on `PLACED`
+  orders.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### Reserve
+
+1. A new reservation is `ACTIVE`, has `order_id` `None`, and has
+   `expires_at` equal to `clock.now()` at reserve time plus the hold length.
+2. The hold length defaults to 20 minutes. It can be configured without
+   breaking the three-argument constructor.
+3. Reservation IDs are sequential: `RES-0001`, `RES-0002`, …
+4. Reserve is **not** all-or-nothing. Each requested line holds
+   `min(requested, available right now)` units.
+5. A line with 0 available is left out of `items` entirely. It does not
+   appear with a value of 0.
+6. If no line can hold any units, reserve raises `InsufficientStock` and
+   creates nothing.
+7. Validation matches `place_order`:
+   - an unknown warehouse raises `UnknownWarehouse`;
+   - an unknown SKU raises `UnknownSku`;
+   - a zero, negative or non-integer quantity raises `InvalidQuantity`;
+   - empty `items` raises an `InventoryError`.
+8. A request rejected for any reason holds nothing, not even for its valid
+   lines, and creates no reservation.
+9. An empty `idempotency_key` raises an `InventoryError` and creates nothing.
+10. Holds never write to the ledger and never change on-hand.
+
+### Idempotency
+
+11. Idempotency keys are global across all warehouses and are remembered for
+    the life of the service.
+12. A call is the "same request" if it has the same warehouse and the same
+    **requested** items as the first call with that key. Item order doesn't
+    matter. The comparison uses what was requested, not what ended up held.
+13. Reserving again with a known key and the same request returns the
+    original reservation in its current state, whether that is `ACTIVE`,
+    `EXPIRED`, `RELEASED` or `CONFIRMED`. The retry creates no new hold,
+    does not change `items`, and does not move `expires_at`.
+14. Reserving again with a known key but a different warehouse or different
+    items raises `IdempotencyConflict`, even if the original reservation is
+    finished. Nothing is created or changed.
+15. A reserve call that failed leaves no trace under its key, so a later
+    call with that key is treated as new.
+
+### Availability
+
+16. While a hold is active, `available` for that SKU and warehouse is reduced
+    by the held units. Holds in one warehouse never affect another warehouse.
+17. `allocated()` and `on_hand()` ignore holds.
+18. `place_order` stays all-or-nothing and can only take available stock,
+    which means stock minus active holds.
+19. Once `clock.now() >= expires_at`, the held units count as available again
+    without any sweep, and the reservation is reported as `EXPIRED`. This
+    includes the moment exactly at `expires_at`.
+20. `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds. If a write-off leaves
+    on-hand below what is held, `available` shows 0 and the reservations stay
+    unchanged.
+
+### Confirm
+
+21. Confirming an active reservation creates a `PLACED` order. The order has:
+    - a new sequential `ORD-` id;
+    - `placed_at` equal to the confirm time;
+    - one line per SKU in the reservation's `items`, with exactly the held
+      quantities.
+
+    After a partial hold, the order covers only the units that were held.
+22. The reservation becomes `CONFIRMED` and its `order_id` is set to the new
+    order's id.
+23. Confirm does not check stock again. The held units become the order's
+    allocation, so `available` is the same just before and just after
+    confirm. On-hand changes only when the order ships.
+24. Confirming a reservation that is already `CONFIRMED` returns the same
+    order and creates nothing. This also applies after its `expires_at` has
+    passed.
+25. Confirming a lapsed reservation raises `ReservationExpired` and creates
+    no order. This includes confirming exactly at `expires_at`.
+26. Confirming a `RELEASED` reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`.
+
+### Release
+
+27. Releasing an `ACTIVE` reservation sets it to `RELEASED` and frees its
+    units at once.
+28. Releasing a `RELEASED` reservation changes nothing and returns the
+    reservation.
+29. Releasing a lapsed reservation changes nothing and returns it with
+    status `EXPIRED`.
+30. Releasing a `CONFIRMED` reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`,
+    and the order is untouched.
+
+### Lookup
+
+31. `get_reservation` returns the reservation with its status as of
+    `clock.now()`, so a lapsed reservation shows as `EXPIRED`.
+32. An unknown reservation id raises `ReservationNotFound` from
+    `get_reservation`, `confirm_reservation` and `release_reservation`.
+
+### Compatibility
+
+33. All existing behaviour and tests stay unchanged. This includes
+    `stock_report` and `StockRow`, which keep their current four columns;
+    their `available` reflects holds.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Extending or refreshing a hold.
+- Holds that span more than one warehouse.
+- A background sweep or scheduled expiry job.
+- A `held` column in `stock_report`, or any other new reporting.
+- Releasing a reservation does not cancel its order; use `cancel_order`.
+  Cancelling or shipping that order does not change the reservation.
+- Expiring idempotency keys or scoping them per warehouse.
+- Persistence beyond the existing in-memory repository.
